IMPORT prelude

-- Railways Act 1905 (Singapore) -- what the Act applies to (s 1), the railway's liability as a carrier of goods, animals, vehicles,
-- luggage and valuables and the limits on it (ss 36 to 45 and the Schedule), and the passenger and public offences (ss 62 to 90).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/RA1905.txt, with amendments to
-- Act 21 of 2025 (in force 17 August 2026, ss 86 and 87) shown; S 40/2022 and Act 25 of 2021 also annotated. The arrangement of
-- sections at the top of the deposit is out of step with the body; the BODY's section numbers are used throughout.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 11 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the provisions a passenger, a
-- consignor or a member of the public meets. Not encoded: construction, land and works (Part 2), opening and inspection (Part 3),
-- returns, property tax and legal proceedings (Parts 4 to 6), accidents (Part 8), the general rules, rates and the manager's
-- disciplinary fines (ss 55 to 61), detention and sale of goods for unpaid sums (s 72), occupation crossings (s 81), recovery and
-- costs (ss 91 to 97), and motor or aircraft services (Part 10).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Railways Act 1905 -- carriage and offences`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `1 -- application`

-- s 1: the Act "shall apply to all railways in Singapore, except a rapid transit system the construction and operation of which is
-- subject to the Rapid Transit Systems Act 1995, and a cross-border railway ... subject to the Cross-Border Railways Act 2018".
DECLARE Railway IS ONE OF
    `an ordinary railway in Singapore`
    `a rapid transit system under the Rapid Transit Systems Act 1995`
    `a cross-border railway under the Cross-Border Railways Act 2018`

GIVEN `the railway` IS A Railway
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Railways Act applies` IF
    CONSIDER `the railway`
    WHEN `an ordinary railway in Singapore` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `36 -- goods: negligence and booking`

-- s 36: the railway administration "shall in no case be liable for loss or injury to any articles or goods ... unless the loss or
-- injury has been caused by negligence or misconduct on the part of its agents or employees, and unless the articles or goods ...
-- have been booked and paid for".
GIVEN `caused by negligence or misconduct of its agents or employees` IS A BOOLEAN, `booked and paid for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the railway can be liable for the goods` IF
    `caused by negligence or misconduct of its agents or employees` AND `booked and paid for`

§§ `37 -- animals`

-- s 37(1): liability for animals "shall not in any case exceed, in the case of horses, $350 a head, or in the case of mules, donkeys
-- or horned cattle, $100 a head, or in the case of sheep, goats, dogs or other animals, $20 a head, unless" a higher value was
-- declared at delivery. (2): the railway may then charge a percentage on the excess.
-- (3): never liable for loss "due to fright or restiveness not caused by negligence or misconduct" of a railway official, nor for
-- delay not so caused.
-- INFERENCE: where a higher value was declared, s 37 sets no cap; the encoding then returns the loss (proof of value under s 43(2)
-- is not modelled).
DECLARE Animal IS ONE OF
    `a horse`
    `a mule`
    `a donkey`
    `a head of horned cattle`
    `a sheep`
    `a goat`
    `a dog`
    `another animal`

GIVEN `the animal` IS A Animal
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the per-head limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the animal`
    WHEN `a horse` THEN 350
    WHEN `a mule` THEN 100
    WHEN `a donkey` THEN 100
    WHEN `a head of horned cattle` THEN 100
    OTHERWISE 20

GIVEN `the animal` IS A Animal, `heads` IS A NUMBER, `higher value declared` IS A BOOLEAN, `the loss` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the compensation for animals` MEANS
    IF `higher value declared`
    THEN `the loss`
    ELSE `the lesser of` `the loss` (`heads` TIMES `the per-head limit` `the animal`)

GIVEN `due to fright, restiveness or delay` IS A BOOLEAN, `caused by negligence or misconduct of a railway official` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the animal claim is barred` IF
    `due to fright, restiveness or delay` AND (NOT `caused by negligence or misconduct of a railway official`)

§§ `38 -- vehicles`

-- s 38(1): no liability for a vehicle "unless that vehicle has been delivered into the custody of a railway clerk or station master
-- and a written acknowledgment of the receipt ... has been obtained".
-- (2): per vehicle limits: (a) traction engine or motor car $200; (b) coach, carriage, ghari or omnibus $100; (c) motor-bicycle or
-- motor-tricycle $50; (d) any other vehicle $10 -- except where a higher value was declared in writing at delivery AND the sender
-- "paid ... a sum ... equal to 1% upon the excess of the value so declared over the limit".
-- (3): "vehicle" includes carts, wagons, vans, lorries, trishaws, bicycles, tricycles, handcarts.
-- INFERENCE: with a declaration and the 1% paid, the encoding takes the declared value as the cap.
DECLARE Vehicle IS ONE OF
    `a motor car`
    `a traction engine`
    `a coach, carriage, ghari or omnibus`
    `a motor-bicycle or motor-tricycle`
    `a lorry`
    `a bicycle`
    `a trishaw`
    `a handcart`

GIVEN `the vehicle` IS A Vehicle
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the vehicle limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the vehicle`
    WHEN `a motor car` THEN 200
    WHEN `a traction engine` THEN 200
    WHEN `a coach, carriage, ghari or omnibus` THEN 100
    WHEN `a motor-bicycle or motor-tricycle` THEN 50
    OTHERWISE 10

GIVEN `delivered into the custody of a railway clerk or station master` IS A BOOLEAN, `written acknowledgment obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the railway can be liable for the vehicle` IF
    `delivered into the custody of a railway clerk or station master` AND `written acknowledgment obtained`

GIVEN `the vehicle` IS A Vehicle, `declared value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the increased-risk charge for the vehicle` MEANS
    IF `declared value` GREATER THAN `the vehicle limit` `the vehicle`
    THEN (`declared value` MINUS `the vehicle limit` `the vehicle`) DIVIDED BY 100
    ELSE 0

GIVEN `the vehicle` IS A Vehicle, `declared in writing and 1% paid` IS A BOOLEAN, `declared value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the vehicle cap` MEANS
    IF `declared in writing and 1% paid` AND `declared value` GREATER THAN `the vehicle limit` `the vehicle`
    THEN `declared value`
    ELSE `the vehicle limit` `the vehicle`

§§ `39 -- passengers' luggage`

-- s 39(1): no responsibility for luggage "unless it has been delivered into the custody of a railway official and retained in the
-- sole custody of the railway administration"; luggage "placed at the request of a passenger in the compartment in which he intends
-- to travel shall be deemed not to be retained in the sole custody".
-- (2): per article and its contents, "whether that article was registered or not": 1st class $100; 2nd class $50; 3rd class $25,
-- unless the value was declared and a percentage on the excess paid.
DECLARE `Ticket class` IS ONE OF
    `first class`
    `second class`
    `third class`

GIVEN `the class` IS A `Ticket class`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the class rank` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the class`
    WHEN `first class` THEN 1
    WHEN `second class` THEN 2
    OTHERWISE 3

GIVEN `delivered to a railway official` IS A BOOLEAN, `kept in the railway's sole custody` IS A BOOLEAN, `placed in the passenger's compartment at his request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the railway can be liable for the luggage` IF
    `delivered to a railway official` AND `kept in the railway's sole custody` AND (NOT `placed in the passenger's compartment at his request`)

GIVEN `the class` IS A `Ticket class`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the luggage limit per article` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the class`
    WHEN `first class` THEN 100
    WHEN `second class` THEN 50
    OTHERWISE 25

GIVEN `the class` IS A `Ticket class`, `value declared and percentage paid` IS A BOOLEAN, `the loss` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the compensation for an article of luggage` MEANS
    IF `value declared and percentage paid`
    THEN `the loss`
    ELSE `the lesser of` `the loss` (`the luggage limit per article` `the class`)

§§ `40 and the Schedule -- articles of special value`

-- s 40(1): where a parcel contains articles in the Schedule (gold and silver, jewellery, watches, securities, bank notes, works of
-- art, glass and china, silks, furs, opium, musical and scientific instruments and others) "and the value of such articles ...
-- exceeds $100, the railway administration shall not be responsible beyond that sum" unless value and contents were declared (and,
-- if required, a percentage paid). (2): if declared, compensation "shall not exceed the value so declared", and the claimant bears
-- the burden of proving it was the true value. (4): not for parcels carried "for any postal authority".
-- INFERENCE: where the section does not apply, the encoding returns the loss uncapped by s 40 (s 39 may still cap luggage).
GIVEN `contains Schedule articles` IS A BOOLEAN, `value of those articles` IS A NUMBER, `value and contents declared` IS A BOOLEAN, `declared value` IS A NUMBER, `carried for a postal authority` IS A BOOLEAN, `the loss` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the compensation for a parcel` MEANS
    IF `carried for a postal authority`
    THEN `the loss`
    ELSE IF `value and contents declared`
         THEN `the lesser of` `the loss` `declared value`
         ELSE IF `contains Schedule articles` AND `value of those articles` GREATER THAN 100
              THEN `the lesser of` `the loss` 100
              ELSE `the loss`

§§ `41 -- through booking by rail and sea`

-- s 41(1): a condition exempting the railway for losses at sea "from the act of God, the State's enemies, fire, accidents from
-- machinery ... and all ... dangers and accidents of the seas" is "deemed to be part of the contract" without being expressed.
-- (2): otherwise liable for losses at sea without its actual fault or privity "to the following extent only": (a) loss of life or
-- personal injury, alone or with goods -- aggregate not exceeding $125 for each ton of the vessel; (b) animals, luggage or goods --
-- not exceeding $60 for each ton [both S 40/2022]. (3): gross tonnage for a steam vessel, registered tonnage for a sailing vessel.
-- (4): one limit per "distinct occasion" however many people suffer. (5): the railway bears the burden of proving the loss happened at sea.
GIVEN `a steam vessel` IS A BOOLEAN, `gross tonnage` IS A NUMBER, `registered tonnage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tonnage counted` MEANS
    IF `a steam vessel` THEN `gross tonnage` ELSE `registered tonnage`

GIVEN `tons` IS A NUMBER, `loss of life or personal injury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the aggregate limit for the occasion` MEANS
    IF `loss of life or personal injury` THEN `tons` TIMES 125 ELSE `tons` TIMES 60

GIVEN `tons` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the limit for animals, luggage or goods at sea` MEANS
    `tons` TIMES 60

§§ `43 and 44 -- proof and the time for claims`

-- s 43(1): "it shall not be necessary for the claimant to prove how the loss, destruction or deterioration was caused" [Act 25 of
-- 2021]; (2): the claimant must prove the value and the extent of the injury.
-- s 44: no refund of an overcharge, and no compensation for animals or goods, "unless his claim ... has been preferred in writing ...
-- within 6 months from the date of the delivery of the animals or goods for carriage". Elapsed time is counted in whole months here.
GIVEN `claim made in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `months after delivery` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim is in time` IF
    `claim made in writing` AND `months after delivery` AT MOST 6

§§ `45 -- goods falsely described`

-- s 45(1): no responsibility for goods "with respect to the description of which a materially false account has been given ... if the
-- loss ... is in any way brought about by the false account". (2): never more than the value calculated on the false description.
GIVEN `a materially false account was given` IS A BOOLEAN, `the loss was in any way brought about by it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the false account bars the claim` IF
    `a materially false account was given` AND `the loss was in any way brought about by it`

GIVEN `a materially false account was given` IS A BOOLEAN, `value on the false description` IS A NUMBER, `the loss` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the compensation for falsely described goods` MEANS
    IF `a materially false account was given`
    THEN `the lesser of` `the loss` `value on the false description`
    ELSE `the loss`

§ `Passengers and the public`

§§ `62 -- travelling without a ticket`

-- s 62(1): no person shall enter a carriage to travel "without first having paid his fare and obtained a ticket".
-- (3): a person travelling without a ticket, or not producing or delivering it up, must pay (a) the fare for the distance travelled
-- (or from where the train originally started, if in doubt) "and in addition (b) a special charge of 50 cents, 25 cents or 10 cents
-- according as he travelled in a carriage ... of the 1st, 2nd or 3rd class". (4) and s 95: enforceable like a fine.
GIVEN `the class` IS A `Ticket class`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the special charge` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the class`
    WHEN `first class` THEN 0.5
    WHEN `second class` THEN 0.25
    OTHERWISE 0.1

GIVEN `the fare` IS A NUMBER, `the class` IS A `Ticket class`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the sum due from a passenger without a ticket` MEANS
    `the fare` PLUS `the special charge` `the class`

§§ `63 -- who gets on when the train is full`

-- s 63(1): fares are accepted "only upon condition that there is room". (2): "those passengers who have obtained tickets for the
-- longest distance shall have the preference", and for the same distance, "according to the order in which they have received their
-- tickets". (3): officers and troops on duty and persons on Government business have priority "without reference to the distance ...
-- or the order".
GIVEN `A on Government business` IS A BOOLEAN, `A distance` IS A NUMBER, `A ticket order` IS A NUMBER, `B on Government business` IS A BOOLEAN, `B distance` IS A NUMBER, `B ticket order` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `A has preference over B` IF
    IF `A on Government business` AND (NOT `B on Government business`)
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE IF `B on Government business` AND (NOT `A on Government business`)
         THEN FALSE
         ELSE IF `A distance` GREATER THAN `B distance`
              THEN TRUE
              ELSE IF `A distance` LESS THAN `B distance`
                   THEN FALSE
                   ELSE `A ticket order` LESS THAN `B ticket order`

§§ `66 -- riding on the engine or in the luggage van`

-- s 66: any person "other than the engineman and fireman and assistant fireman" who without the special licence of the manager or
-- locomotive superintendent rides on a locomotive or tender, and any person "other than the guard or brakesman" who without special
-- permission rides in a luggage van or goods wagon -- fine not exceeding $40.
DECLARE Rider IS ONE OF
    `the engineman`
    `the fireman`
    `the assistant fireman`
    `the guard`
    `the brakesman`
    `a passenger`

GIVEN `the rider` IS A Rider, `has the special licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `riding on the engine is an offence` IF
    (NOT `has the special licence`) AND
    (CONSIDER `the rider`
     WHEN `the engineman` THEN FALSE
     WHEN `the fireman` THEN FALSE
     WHEN `the assistant fireman` THEN FALSE
     OTHERWISE TRUE)

GIVEN `the rider` IS A Rider, `has special permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `riding in the luggage van is an offence` IF
    (NOT `has special permission`) AND
    (CONSIDER `the rider`
     WHEN `the guard` THEN FALSE
     WHEN `the brakesman` THEN FALSE
     OTHERWISE TRUE)

§§ `70 -- being directed to another carriage`

-- s 70(1): a passenger may be directed to travel in any carriage the official indicates, "not being of a lower class than that for
-- which he has paid his fare". (2): refusing a valid direction -- removal and forfeiture of the fare.
GIVEN `class paid for` IS A `Ticket class`, `class directed to` IS A `Ticket class`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the direction is valid` IF
    `the class rank` `class directed to` AT MOST `the class rank` `class paid for`

§§ `62 to 90 -- maximum penalties`

-- ss 64 to 90, each "shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding" (and for some, imprisonment):
-- s 64 fraud on fares, $100 "for each offence"; s 65 boarding or leaving a moving carriage, or riding on the steps, $20; s 66 riding on
-- the engine or in the luggage van, $40; s 67 smoking, spitting or chewing betel where prohibited, $20; s 68 intoxication, nuisance or
-- interfering with comfort, $40 or 3 months or both; s 69 improper use of the emergency signal, $100; s 71 entering a women-only or
-- reserved carriage, or staying in a higher class, $100; s 74 carrying a dangerous article, $200; s 75 travelling knowing oneself to
-- have a contagious disease, $500; s 76 removing survey stakes, $40; s 77(1) trespass, $20; s 77(2) refusing to leave, $40; s 78
-- driving an animal across the line, $40; s 79 defacing a ticket, $100; s 80 obstructing a railway employee, $200; s 83(1) damaging
-- railway property, $200 or one year; s 84 gates left open, $100; s 85 causing a train to stop, $200; s 86 obstructing the line or
-- throwing things at trains with intent, $1,000 or 20 YEARS or both [Act 21 of 2025]; s 87 wilful act endangering safety, $200 or 7
-- YEARS or both [Act 21 of 2025]; s 89 rash or negligent act, $100 or 6 months or both; s 90 breach of rules, $20.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `fare fraud`
    `boarding a moving carriage`
    `riding on the engine`
    `smoking where prohibited`
    `intoxication or nuisance`
    `improper use of the emergency signal`
    `entering a reserved carriage`
    `carrying a dangerous article`
    `travelling with a contagious disease`
    `removing survey stakes`
    `trespass`
    `refusing to leave when asked`
    `driving an animal across the line`
    `defacing a ticket`
    `obstructing a railway employee`
    `damaging railway property`
    `leaving a crossing gate open`
    `causing a train to stop`
    `obstructing the line with intent`
    `wilfully endangering safety`
    `a rash or negligent act`
    `breach of the rules`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `fare fraud` THEN 100
    WHEN `boarding a moving carriage` THEN 20
    WHEN `riding on the engine` THEN 40
    WHEN `smoking where prohibited` THEN 20
    WHEN `intoxication or nuisance` THEN 40
    WHEN `improper use of the emergency signal` THEN 100
    WHEN `entering a reserved carriage` THEN 100
    WHEN `carrying a dangerous article` THEN 200
    WHEN `travelling with a contagious disease` THEN 500
    WHEN `removing survey stakes` THEN 40
    WHEN `trespass` THEN 20
    WHEN `refusing to leave when asked` THEN 40
    WHEN `driving an animal across the line` THEN 40
    WHEN `defacing a ticket` THEN 100
    WHEN `obstructing a railway employee` THEN 200
    WHEN `damaging railway property` THEN 200
    WHEN `leaving a crossing gate open` THEN 100
    WHEN `causing a train to stop` THEN 200
    WHEN `obstructing the line with intent` THEN 1000
    WHEN `wilfully endangering safety` THEN 200
    WHEN `a rash or negligent act` THEN 100
    OTHERWISE 20

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `intoxication or nuisance` THEN 3
    WHEN `damaging railway property` THEN 12
    WHEN `obstructing the line with intent` THEN 240
    WHEN `wilfully endangering safety` THEN 84
    WHEN `a rash or negligent act` THEN 6
    OTHERWISE 0

§§ `67, 68, 70, 71 -- forfeiting the fare`

-- s 67(3): a person who "persists in infringing this section, after being warned to desist" may be removed and "shall, if a
-- passenger, forfeit his fare". s 68(2): an intoxicated or indecent offender, likewise. s 70(2): refusing a valid direction to a
-- carriage. s 71: entering a reserved carriage, likewise. No forfeiture is attached to fare fraud (s 64) or a first smoking offence.
DECLARE Conduct IS ONE OF
    `smoking once without a warning`
    `smoking on after a warning`
    `travelling while intoxicated`
    `refusing a valid direction to a carriage`
    `staying in a women-only compartment`
    `riding beyond the station paid for`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the passenger forfeits the fare` IF
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `smoking once without a warning` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `riding beyond the station paid for` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `73, 75, 82 -- penalties that scale`

-- s 73(2): failing to give, or wilfully falsifying, a written account of goods -- "a fine not exceeding $40 for every ton of goods and
-- to a fine not exceeding $20 for any quantity of goods less than a ton" [S 40/2022]. (3): not for passengers' luggage. The encoding
-- reads whole tons only; how a fraction above one ton is counted is not said.
-- s 75(4): a railway company that fails to disinfect a carriage "shall forfeit to the Government the sum of $20 for every day".
-- s 82(1): the owner of an animal that strays onto the railway, "such railway or lands being provided with suitable fences for
-- excluding cattle", is liable to a fine not exceeding $10 for each animal. INFERENCE: unfenced, no offence (returned as 0).
GIVEN `tons of goods` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for no or a false account of goods` MEANS
    IF `tons of goods` LESS THAN 1 THEN 20 ELSE `tons of goods` TIMES 40

GIVEN `days in default` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the sum forfeited for not disinfecting` MEANS
    `days in default` TIMES 20

GIVEN `the railway was suitably fenced` IS A BOOLEAN, `animals` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for straying animals` MEANS
    IF `the railway was suitably fenced` THEN `animals` TIMES 10 ELSE 0
